WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Speaker 1: We have a really interesting&nbsp;
political situation that surfaced in the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.640
24 to 48 hours, a poll came out from the&nbsp;
perennially unreliable Rasmussen Reports,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.880
which says that if the 20 24 election were held&nbsp;
today and Donald Trump were the Republican nominee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.400
and Joe Biden were the Democratic nominee,&nbsp;
Donald Trump would defeat Biden by 10 points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:29.040
51 to 41. Now, what is interesting about this,&nbsp;
other than, you know, it's three years out and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.120
poll right now is sort of meaningless. There&nbsp;
are two things that are very interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.640
One is I don't actually disagree with the&nbsp;
general conclusion. And that conclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.840
is that Donald Trump might easily win in 2024&nbsp;
against Joe Biden. I've actually said before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:51.920
when I think about 20, 24 big picture, I don't&nbsp;
really see Joe Biden at age 81 days short of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.800
80 second birthday in November of twenty twenty&nbsp;
four, defeating Donald Trump after four years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.880
of Trump talking about how terrible Joe&nbsp;
Biden is, I see it as a big uphill battle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:12.240
If Biden says no thanks, I'm not running for&nbsp;
reelection. But Kamala Harris is the nominee as of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:18.320
right now. Kamala Harris, his approval rating is&nbsp;
not good. And I don't see Kamala defeating Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:25.200
Trump in a general election either. And that's why&nbsp;
I've been saying the best scenario is Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.840
not running in twenty, twenty four. But that&nbsp;
doesn't change that. This poll, a Rasmussen poll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:38.720
three years out, is really not worth much at&nbsp;
all. But all the normal stuff starts happening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.560
when the poll comes out. The Washington&nbsp;
Examiner starts writing headlines about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:52.880
the poll. Trump over Biden by 10 points, Harris&nbsp;
by 13. Trump then publishes a reference on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:59.840
website to the poll and a link to this very same&nbsp;
Washington Examiner article. And the ecosystem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:06.000
starts to repeat itself and build on itself.&nbsp;
So this is a sort of weird situation because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:13.840
I think Trump could absolutely win in 2024,&nbsp;
but without knowing what happens in 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.520
and what the next, you know, at least 18&nbsp;
months of the Joe Biden presidency look like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:25.760
it is very hard to say anything substantive about&nbsp;
the specifics of Trump vs. Biden in twenty 24&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.560
hour Republican voters ignorant enough to elect&nbsp;
Donald Trump again. Absolutely. Of course they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:37.600
are. Which is why it would be better for Donald&nbsp;
Trump not to run. And whatever that reason is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.360
Trump becoming convinced that he can't win.&nbsp;
When I was on the Michael Cohen podcast a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.640
few weeks ago or maybe six weeks ago,&nbsp;
something like that, Michael Cohen said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.960
I don't think Trump will run because he can't&nbsp;
handle another disappointment. He can't handle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.880
another hit to his ego. He just he just can't&nbsp;
handle it. And so he doesn't want the chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.120
of losing again and he's not going to run. But&nbsp;
at the same time, Trump is a major narcissist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.760
and it takes a lot for Trump to think he can't&nbsp;
win. Trump tends to think he can win. He tends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.560
to think of himself as invincible. And that, to&nbsp;
me, signals that he very well may run unless it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.200
abundantly clear that he has no shot. It would&nbsp;
be better for Trump not to run because there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.760
no question that the American public, as a result&nbsp;
of its composition, with so many low information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:25.200
radicalized Republicans would vote for Trump&nbsp;
again, at least plausibly. The message here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:31.840
is that the exact coalition that brought&nbsp;
Biden his victory in 2020, which came down to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.920
not that many votes in a few states,&nbsp;
remember massive popular vote victory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:44.400
bigger margin than Trump when it came&nbsp;
to electoral, not in electoral votes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.480
but the combined margin in the states that made a&nbsp;
difference. It was a few hundred thousand rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:56.400
than just the 77000 votes in three states that&nbsp;
pushed Trump over 270. But Biden's coalition was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:02.160
very precarious. A slight departure from it could&nbsp;
have seen Donald Trump reelected. And that's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:08.480
a threat that should be understated. So do&nbsp;
we care about Rasmussen three years out? No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:14.880
not specifically. The polling is bogus, but the&nbsp;
message that Trump could definitely win in 2024&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.880
is an accurate message, and that's the&nbsp;
one that we should be paying attention to.

